 ## Unreleased — 1.4.0
 
-Nothing yet.
+### Changed
+
+- **`smysl fmt` skips its round-trip reparse when nothing changed.** The guard that re-parses
+  formatted text and refuses to emit anything whose records or labels moved now only runs when
+  `write_surface` actually produced text different from the input — when it is byte-identical,
+  it is the same string `parse_surface` already read to build `out`, so a second parse could
+  only recompute `out.labels`/`out.records`, never disagree with them. An already-canonical
+  tree under `fmt --check`, or a second `fmt --write`, now costs one parse per file instead of
+  two. Behaviour is unchanged; only files `fmt` actually rewrites still pay for the reparse.
 
 ---
 
